                <pb facs="0330" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg258"/>

                <head>No. 42.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 5,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 3d instant, requesting that Mr. Patrick Slattery, a
                    naturalized citizen of the United States, who is detained in Limerick County
                    jail, under the; protection of person and property (Ireland) act, 1881, may be
                    brought to trial at an early date.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to state to you that I have referred this matter to
                    the proper department of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
